WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:17.828
dropping the jewel, Swallow felt wonderful.

2
00:00:17.848 --> 00:00:22.629
"I'm so glad I stayed to help the prince," he thought.

3
00:00:22.649 --> 00:00:24.990
"And the seamstress.

4
00:00:27.291 --> 00:00:29.171
Now it's time to leave for Egypt."

5
00:00:30.511 --> 00:00:32.112
Swallow began flying east.

6
00:00:33.988 --> 00:00:35.029
But he wasn't alone.

7
00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:38.351
A large hawk was flying right above him.

8
00:00:42.574 --> 00:00:43.995
no!" Swallow thought.

9
00:00:44.015 --> 00:00:47.778
"That hawk looks hungry!"

10
00:00:49.359 --> 00:00:52.642
Swoosh! Swallow switched directions and flew back to town.

11
00:00:54.843 --> 00:00:56.144
The hawk did not follow him.

12
00:00:56.164 --> 00:01:01.268
"Phew! That was scary," Swallow thought.

13
00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.521
He was about to begin the journey again.

14
00:01:05.921 --> 00:01:08.682
Suddenly he heard a long, deep moan.

15
00:01:08.702 --> 00:01:10.843
"That's Prince!

16
00:01:11.784 --> 00:01:12.564
Is he in trouble?"

17
00:01:14.885 --> 00:01:15.985
Swallow zoomed back.

18
00:01:17.246 --> 00:01:18.987
The statue was crying again.

19
00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:26.430
Why are you sad?"

20
00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:27.690
Swallow asked.

21
00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:31.372
"The seamstress was so grateful for the jewel.

22
00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.881
Now she can buy her son's medicine."

23
00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:38.582
"Thank you."

24
00:01:40.723 --> 00:01:41.884
The statue sniffed.

25
00:01:41.904 --> 00:01:46.426
"But there are so many more people like her.

26
00:01:47.866 --> 00:01:50.768
Poor, sick, and unhappy."

27
00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:57.411
Swallow sighed.

28
00:01:57.431 --> 00:02:00.432
"What if I help someone else?

29
00:02:01.772 --> 00:02:02.953
Would that make you feel better?"

30
00:02:02.973 --> 00:02:05.495
"What about Egypt?"

31
00:02:05.515 --> 00:02:09.419
"I will go tomorrow," Swallow said.

32
00:02:09.439 --> 00:02:12.401
"I can't leave while you're so sad."

33
00:02:16.185 --> 00:02:19.507
The next day Swallow plucked the other ruby from the statue's belt.

34
00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:22.930
Then he flew to the docks by the river.

35
00:02:26.493 --> 00:02:29.196
At one dock a captain was talking to his crew.

36
00:02:30.604 --> 00:02:32.106
"Finish loading the ship.

37
00:02:33.187 --> 00:02:35.389
We set sail for Egypt today!"

38
00:02:35.409 --> 00:02:38.872
"That's where I'm going!"

39
00:02:39.252 --> 00:02:40.093
Swallow thought.

40
00:02:41.114 --> 00:02:41.754
"See you there!

41
00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.957
But first, my errand for the prince."

42
00:02:46.819 --> 00:02:50.843
Swallow swooped through crowds, past mothers with crying children.

43
00:02:52.845 --> 00:02:55.948
He picked up breadcrumbs and dropped them for hungry dogs.

44
00:03:00.476 --> 00:03:02.498
"Everyone needs something," he thought.

45
00:03:02.518 --> 00:03:05.060
"But I can't help everyone.

46
00:03:06.442 --> 00:03:08.403
I need to find the person I'm looking for.

47
00:03:08.423 --> 00:03:11.907
Then I'll leave for Egypt, just like that ship."

48
00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:17.051
At last, Swallow spotted her.

49
00:03:18.432 --> 00:03:21.855
He dove through the crowd and landed near a young girl.

50
00:03:24.017 --> 00:03:26.420
She wore a thin sweater and was shivering.

51
00:03:27.572 --> 00:03:30.273
In her hands she held a basket of eggs.

52
00:03:30.293 --> 00:03:33.234
"Eggs for sale!

53
00:03:34.394 --> 00:03:37.235
Please, buy my eggs," she called.

54
00:03:38.575 --> 00:03:40.736
A woman stopped and curled her lip.

55
00:03:42.596 --> 00:03:44.837
"No one will buy broken eggs!"

56
00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:48.318
"But I must sell some!

57
00:03:49.878 --> 00:03:53.459
Or I'll have no money to bring to the orphanage," the girl said.

58
00:03:53.479 --> 00:03:56.380
"Then we'll all go hungry!"

59
00:03:59.532 --> 00:04:01.853
The woman shrugged and walked away.

60
00:04:05.194 --> 00:04:07.155
Swallow felt a pang in his chest.

61
00:04:07.175 --> 00:04:10.916
"How unkind," he thought.

62
00:04:12.777 --> 00:04:14.038
He flew closer to the girl.

63
00:04:15.558 --> 00:04:18.819
Then he carefully dropped the jewel into her basket.
